values.content:
=You are a revenue operations analyst. Analyze the following billing discrepancy and return a JSON object ONLY — no preamble, no markdown, just raw JSON.

Deal Name: {{ $json.dealName }}
Stage: {{ $json.stageName }}
Contracted Amount: ${{ $json.expected }}
Actually Billed: ${{ $json.actual }}
Revenue Gap: ${{ $json.missing }}

Severity rules:
- critical: gap > $10,000
- medium: gap between $1,000 and $10,000
- low: gap < $1,000
Always return one of these three values for severity. Never return "unknown".

Return this exact JSON structure:
{
  "severity": "critical | medium | low",
  "rootCause": "one sentence explaining the likely cause",
  "recommendation": "one sentence on what the finance team should do",
  "auditNote": "a 2-3 sentence note suitable for logging in Salesforce"
}

parameters.jsCode:
const sfData = $('API Rate Limit Delay').item.json;
const sheetItems = items;

const opportunityId = sfData.Id;
const dealId = sfData.AccountId;
const dealName = sfData.Name;
const stageName = sfData.StageName;

const expected = Number(sfData.Amount) || 0;

let actual = 0;
for (const item of sheetItems) {
  if (item.json['Deal ID'] === dealId) {
    actual += Number(item.json['Billed Amount']) || 0;
  }
}

const missing = expected - actual;

if (missing > 0) {
  return [{
    json: {
      opportunityId,
      dealId,
      dealName,
      stageName,
      expected,
      actual,
      missing
    }
  }];
}

return [];

const item = $input.first().json;

// Use emojis and bolding for better readability at a glance
const slackMessage = ` *Revenue Leakage Detected*
*Deal:* ${item.dealName}
*Status:* ${(item.severity || 'unknown').toUpperCase()}

 *Financial Gap:* $${item.missing.toLocaleString()}
(Contracted: $${item.expected.toLocaleString()} | Billed: $${item.actual.toLocaleString()})

*Root Cause:* ${item.rootCause}
*Action:* ${item.recommendation}`;

return {
  ...item,
  slackMessage
};

